{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734690",
      "title": "Lifting State Up",
      "sourceHash": "d4176f20fce7ec5686fc01de37e71eef20f6a306229208a323235b0de1f35f12",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.181,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "[Maximilian] So that's how we can useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 5.94,
          "en": "And the special thing really is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "that when you update your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.23,
          "en": "the component function gets executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.23,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "and therefore the latest JSX snapshot gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "used by React, gets compared to the previous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 21.213,
          "en": "snapshot and the UI is updated where needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 26.58,
          "en": "Now, here, however, the goal was to basically get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.58,
          "end": 30.27,
          "en": "this text into this first post component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.27,
          "end": 32.643,
          "en": "And of course that's not happening right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "One problem we're facing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 39.39,
          "en": "is that this state is inside the NewPost component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.39,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "That's great, but we don't need it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 44.7,
          "en": "Instead, we need it in the PostsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "so that we can set this entered text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 49.023,
          "en": "as a value for this body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 53.373,
          "en": "Now, how do we get the state from NewPost to PostsList?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "Well, an obvious solution would be to import useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 63.15,
          "en": "from React in the PostsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.15,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "and register the state there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 68.61,
          "en": "We could have the EnteredBody here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.61,
          "end": 69.843,
          "en": "with help of useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.7,
          "end": 73.89,
          "en": "And this should use object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.89,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "here to get the EnteredBody",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 79.293,
          "en": "and the set EnteredBody state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "Now we have the state in the component where we need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 86.49,
          "en": "and we could set this body to the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 88.98,
          "en": "that's currently stored in EnteredBody",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.98,
          "end": 92.553,
          "en": "so that our current state value is output down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 97.05,
          "en": "That's amazing and great and theoretically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 100.08,
          "en": "that's a good approach but now we have the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.08,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "in the right place, but the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 104.343,
          "en": "is in a different component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "So how can we solve this puzzle?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "We either have the state or the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 111.63,
          "en": "in the wrong component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "Well, what we have to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 115.62,
          "en": "and what we already started doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 118.743,
          "en": "is something that's called lifting the state up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.58,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "If you have state that's manipulated in component A",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 128.37,
          "en": "but needed in component B, you should lift the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.37,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "up to a component that has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 133.893,
          "en": "to both components that need the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "So in this case, it's the PostsList component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "that needs the state to pass it to post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "as a value for the body prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 146.76,
          "en": "And it's also the PostsList component that has access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.76,
          "end": 148.35,
          "en": "to the NewPost component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.35,
          "end": 151.443,
          "en": "which is the place where the state should be manipulated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "Now what we can do in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "is we can get rid of the state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159.01,
          "en": "in NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 161.85,
          "en": "and get rid of the event handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.85,
          "end": 165.18,
          "en": "and the useState import as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.18,
          "end": 168.6,
          "en": "And we could now simply use this props feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 170.73,
          "en": "So this props object, which we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.73,
          "end": 173.13,
          "en": "by React automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.13,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "to set this onChange event listener prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 179.25,
          "en": "equal to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 180.303,
          "en": "props.onBodyChange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.66,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "Now this prop name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "because you can set any props you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 190.143,
          "en": "on your own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "With that prop being set like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 197.7,
          "en": "on the onChange prop of text area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.7,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "we can go to PostsList and on NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 205.21,
          "en": "we can now add the onBodyChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 208.44,
          "en": "prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.44,
          "end": 210.483,
          "en": "to the NewPost component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 215.55,
          "en": "And as a value we can now again pass in a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.55,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "that should be called when the text area changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "So when the change even occurs on the text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "In this case, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 224.89,
          "en": "the bodyChangeHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "where we automatically get the event object as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 231.87,
          "en": "and where we then call set EnteredBody",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.87,
          "end": 235.92000000000002,
          "en": "equal to event.target.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 235.92000000000002,
          "end": 238.92000000000002,
          "en": "and it's then the bodyChangeHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.92000000000002,
          "end": 242.823,
          "en": "which is passed as a value to onBodyChange, to this prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "Now this might be confusing at first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "but what I'm doing here is I'm passing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 252.3,
          "en": "bodyChangeHandler function to onBodyChange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.3,
          "end": 255.57,
          "en": "So we're not executing it here, we have no parenthesis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.57,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "Instead, I'm using this function bodyChangeHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 263.613,
          "en": "as a value that's passed to the onBodyChange prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.08,
          "end": 266.82,
          "en": "Now in the NewPost component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.82,
          "end": 270.06,
          "en": "I'm then in the end forwarding that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.06,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "that's received on the onBodyChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "as a value to the onChange prop of text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.2,
          "en": "So we simply pass that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 280.2,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "that bodyChangeHandler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "through the NewPost component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "with help of the onBodyChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 289.353,
          "en": "to the text area component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.86,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "And this should all be quite a bit less confusing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 296.73,
          "en": "if you keep in mind that functions can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 296.73,
          "end": 300.843,
          "en": "just like any other kind of value in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.03,
          "end": 304.62,
          "en": "So therefore, in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 304.62,
          "end": 308.31,
          "en": "we wire up this bodyChangeHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.31,
          "end": 311.07,
          "en": "to this change event on text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.07,
          "end": 313.98,
          "en": "That's why we also still get this event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 318.24,
          "en": "And with that we can now update the state in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.24,
          "end": 321.57,
          "en": "where we need it while still setting the listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 321.57,
          "end": 324.123,
          "en": "in the component where the event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 325.636,
          "end": 327.39,
          "en": "And of course, we can also do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.39,
          "end": 329.19,
          "en": "with the author input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.19,
          "end": 331.89,
          "en": "There, we can add the default onChange prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 331.89,
          "end": 335.52,
          "en": "to add a change event listener to that input as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 335.52,
          "end": 339,
          "en": "And for example, expect to get a function value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 341.443,
          "en": "on the onAuthor change prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.79200000000003,
          "end": 344.771,
          "en": "Again, this prop name is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.771,
          "end": 347.071,
          "en": "because it's your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.071,
          "end": 351.181,
          "en": "But with this prop chosen here inside of NewPost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.181,
          "end": 353.995,
          "en": "we now have to use the same prop name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 353.995,
          "end": 358.134,
          "en": "on the NewPost component in PostsList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.134,
          "end": 362.4,
          "en": "and then copy that bodyChangeHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 362.4,
          "end": 366.381,
          "en": "and name this copy authorChangeHandler, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 366.381,
          "end": 369.878,
          "en": "to then pass this authorChangeHandler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 369.878,
          "end": 373.211,
          "en": "as a value to the on author change prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 376.5,
          "en": "And then again, that's picked up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 376.5,
          "end": 379.8,
          "en": "and used as a value for the onChange prop inside of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.8,
          "end": 381.33299999999997,
          "en": "that NewPost component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 383.64,
          "end": 386.52,
          "en": "Now we just need to register a second state slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.52,
          "end": 387.72,
          "en": "for that author name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 387.72,
          "end": 389.94,
          "en": "and that is something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 389.94,
          "end": 393.06,
          "en": "You're not limited to one single state per component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 393.06,
          "end": 396.603,
          "en": "Instead you can have as many state values as you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 397.44,
          "end": 401.01,
          "en": "So here we can simply call useState again to register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.01,
          "end": 404.73,
          "en": "a second state value for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404.73,
          "end": 407.88,
          "en": "And this also is an empty string initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.88,
          "end": 410.90999999999997,
          "en": "but then we get back two values again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 410.90999999999997,
          "end": 415.56,
          "en": "or one value, one array with two elements to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 415.56,
          "end": 417.36,
          "en": "That's my entered author.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.36,
          "end": 420.51,
          "en": "And then my updating function, which could be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 420.51,
          "end": 421.36,
          "en": "setEnteredAuthor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 423.052,
          "end": 426.33,
